{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162979-benevolent-possession","id":162979,"title":"Benevolent Possession","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-08T17:28:21-07:00","id":162979,"title":"Benevolent Possession","content":"In <u>Predators</u> (P.71, 'A Note on Intent'), the possibility for sympathetic possessions is offered up. This presents a number of intriguing story possibilities, but what would be the best way to represent such characters? The Hunter Conspiracy of Les Mysteres suggests a form of minor possession as the basis of their Endowment, but does that really stay true to the themes represented by the Claimed? An alternative would be to employ some form of analog to the new Harmony mechanic from <u>Idigam Chronicles</u>, representing balance between host and rider. Anyone have any other thoughts on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T18:04:32-07:00","id":163023,"title":"","content":"To represent playable claimed, one option would be tweaking the Siten Uzu rules from Skinchangers as that is essentially a form of sympathetic possession. In this case the spirit would be slumbering. I would not recommend a playing someone claimed by a benevolent spirit if the spirit stays active, as the merger between host and spirit is total and final (the character ceases to be 'human' and would thus in most cases still become an NPC).<br /> <br /> To represent someone urged by a sympathetic spirit, you could just use the rules as presented. As there is no reason for this urging to be permanent (the spirit can't even use its Numina and the only reason for urging normally is getting a fleshpuppet to control), I don't think a Harmony like trait is necessary. Just roleplay it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T18:07:41-07:00","id":163025,"title":"","content":"The first thing that comes to mind is a class of spirit whose bans have developed to facilitate such behavior, possibly as part of the agenda of some Incarna or other. Political-occult inroads by powerful members of the Tool Descant might make for an interesting plot, for example, or the <i>siten uzu</i> from Skinchangers could be simply the most prominent class of Claimed who act more like human fetishes than the zenith of spiritual puppetry.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, though, awakened spirits can't be tamed so much as negotiated and possession in the WoD is an invasive process that gets to be damaging to undo once it's reached the point of actual mutation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T18:17:51-07:00","id":163030,"title":"","content":"Are you talking about creating a minor template or something?<br /> <br /> Really you'd just use the rules for spirit-ridden, but with an arrangement, one where the spirit gets the lions share of benefits. The spirit of the fire angel only speaks through Reverend McNally while he's in his church, in front of his congregation, where they can feed it essence. Or the spirit of darkness only rides Zach when he's in his sub-level dorm room, where he's broken all the lights, in exchange he can 'see' in ways he never could before. You'd want to keep in mind that spirits aren't really good Samaritans out to help other people because it makes them warm inside. They want something out of it.<br /> <br /> The Les Mysteres, at their basis, work as the same thing. It's just, from the powers we see, they are oriented around killing werewolves or the hunt, so all their powers kind of encourage that. They also get pack more of a punch, as they're (mostly) dealing with really powerful spirits, not the spirit of that convenience store down the street, but spirits backed by decades or centuries of religious faith, and the lesser spirits in their choirs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T19:45:08-07:00","id":163075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162979-benevolent-possession?p=163030#post163030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Les Mysteres, at their basis, work as the same thing. It's just, from the powers we see, they are oriented around killing werewolves or the hunt, so all their powers kind of encourage that. They also get pack more of a punch, as they're (mostly) dealing with really powerful spirits, not the spirit of that convenience store down the street, but spirits backed by decades or centuries of religious faith, and the lesser spirits in their choirs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Granted that is from a Hunter-Werewolf viewpoint. I've always kinda wondered how the interact when they are not messing with the Uratha. The organization is less &quot;We exist to hunt werewolves&quot; and more &quot;We exist to interact with spirits and werewolves get in the way of that&quot;. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T20:48:42-07:00","id":163097,"title":"","content":"It seems to be a spiritual fulfillment sort of thing. They're modern day shamans (shamen?) without being part spirit, like werewolves.<br /> <br /> They believe the spirits are angels or guardians or simply beings persecuted by the mechanations of werewolves, a variety of things. Their beliefs depend on who taught them, who recruited them.<br /> <br /> So does what they do with their powers, though it suggests they act as sort of spiritual advisors to the community, flat out hunters with an edge, lone medicine men, messiahs bringing the word of the divine spirits to the real world, other things. There's a few different options given but, really, they're people who can channel spirit powers. They're meant to be hunters, but they can do whatever they want, though they likely wouldn't retain the help of the spirits if they refuse to help them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}